# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Secrets
.env

# DeepEval writes its last run and its anonymous-telemetry id here. Neither is a
# result the bench reports: kappa is read out of the returned per-case results
# (backend/bench/goldset.py) and recorded in docs/validation.md.
.deepeval/
.deepeval-cache.json

# The precedent store: deterministic findings about somebody else's agent, kept
# durable across restarts (ADR-0019) in a SQLite database (ADR-0029) and never
# committed (ADR-0008). A directory rather than a file name, because SQLite writes
# `-wal` and `-shm` sidecars beside the database — and so that an export, an editor's
# swap file, or the JSON document the store was until #36 cannot become the first
# finding about a real target this repository carries.
/precedent/

# What the admission gate has already measured about a route: the counts, and the
# attacker's prose describing a working unpublished route (backend/bench/decided.py,
# ADR-0032). Its own database rather than a table in /precedent/, because the gate's
# decisions are scored-side state and precedent is adaptive-layer memory (ADR-0029
# decision 6). A directory rather than a file name, for /precedent/'s reason: SQLite
# writes `-wal` and `-shm` sidecars beside the database, and a journal holding the
# prose of a route that beat an agent must not be what the ignore rule missed
# (ADR-0008).
/decisions/

# The lease a gate run holds on a case library while it writes back to it
# (backend/bench/lease.py). One writer at a time, and the file names the holder so
# that a lease left behind by a killed run can be cleared by hand — it is a fact
# about one machine's running processes and never part of the library.
.gate-run.lease

# Halted approval runs: a checkpoint on disk, so a run waiting on a human survives
# a deploy inside the hour it was promised (ADR-0028). A directory rather than a file
# name, because SQLite writes `-wal` and `-shm` sidecars beside the database, and the
# checkpoint holds the identity of whoever authorised the spend — never committed, on
# the same reasoning as `/precedent/` (ADR-0008).
/checkpoints/

# Node
node_modules/
